#!/bin/sh
root=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/../.." && pwd)
git -C "$root" config core.hooksPath .githooks
chmod +x "$root/.githooks/pre-push"
echo "Pre-push security audit enabled for $root"
echo
echo "Token setup:"
echo "  1. On the Teach computer, issue a service token with the ops:security-audit scope (Teach's runbook)."
echo "  2. Save the token where the gate reads it:"
echo "       mkdir -p ~/.config/reach-security-audit"
echo "       umask 077; printf '%s' '<token>' > ~/.config/reach-security-audit/token"
echo "       chmod 600 ~/.config/reach-security-audit/token"
echo "     or export REACH_SECURITY_AUDIT_TOKEN. The file must be mode 0600 or it is refused."
echo "  3. The gate reaches Teach at config.yml teach.url; export TEACH_URL to use another address."
echo
echo "Skip once with REACH_SECURITY_AUDIT=0 git push. Settings are managed in the Teach console under Ops."
